"kā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"மத்","tr":"mat"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"துப்","tr":"tup"}]},{"text":"பகையே","tr":"pakaiyē","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"பகை","tr":"pakai"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யே","tr":"yē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"வேரும்","parts":[{"text":"வேர்","lemma":"vēr","gloss":"root"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the root"},{"surface":"முதலும்","parts":[{"text":"முதல்","lemma":"mutal","gloss":"trunk"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the trunk"},{"surface":"கோடும்","parts":[{"text":"கோடு","lemma":"kōṭu","gloss":"branch"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the branch"},{"surface":"ஓராங்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஓராங்கு","lemma":"ōrāṅku","gloss":"together"}],"gloss":"together"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தொடுத்த","parts":[{"text":"தொடுத்த","lemma":"toṭu","gloss":"bound"}],"gloss":"bound"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"pōla","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"தூங்குபு","parts":[{"text":"தூங்குபு","lemma":"tūṅku","gloss":"hanging"}],"gloss":"hanging"},{"surface":"தொடரி","parts":[{"text":"தொடரி","lemma":"toṭar","gloss":"linked"}],"gloss":"linked continuously"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கீழ்","parts":[{"text":"கீழ்","lemma":"kīḻ","gloss":"downward"}],"gloss":"downward"},{"surface":"தாழ்வன்ன","parts":[{"text":"தாழ்வு","lemma":"tāḻvu","gloss":"hanging low"},{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"aṉṉa","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like hanging low"},{"surface":"வீழ்கோள்","parts":[{"text":"வீழ்","lemma":"vīḻ","gloss":"descending"},{"text":"கோள்","lemma":"koḷ","gloss":"bearing fruit"}],"gloss":"bearing fruit on low roots"},{"surface":"பலவின்","parts":[{"text":"பலவு","lemma":"palavu","gloss":"jackfruit tree"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the jackfruit tree"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆர்கலி","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்","lemma":"ār","gloss":"roaring"},{"text":"கலி","lemma":"kali","gloss":"sound"}],"gloss":"roaring sound"},{"surface":"வெற்பன்","parts":[{"text":"வெற்பன்","lemma":"verpaṉ","gloss":"lord of the mountain"}],"gloss":"lord of the mountain"},{"surface":"வருதொறும்","parts":[{"text":"வரு","lemma":"varu","gloss":"come"},{"text":"தொறும்","lemma":"toṟum","gloss":"whenever"}],"gloss":"whenever he comes"},{"surface":"வரூஉம்","parts":[{"text":"வரூஉம்","lemma":"varu","gloss":"comes"}],"gloss":"comes"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அகலினும்","parts":[{"text":"அகலின்","lemma":"akal","gloss":"if departs"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even if he departs"},{"surface":"அகலாதாகி","parts":[{"text":"அகலாது","lemma":"akalātu","gloss":"not departing"},{"text":"ஆகி","lemma":"āki","gloss":"becoming"}],"gloss":"without leaving"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இகலும்","parts":[{"text":"இகலும்","lemma":"ikal","gloss":"contends"}],"gloss":"contends"},{"surface":"தோழி","parts":[{"text":"தோழி","lemma":"tōḻi","gloss":"friend"}],"gloss":"O friend"},{"surface":"நம்","parts":[{"text":"நம்","lemma":"nam","gloss":"our"}],"gloss":"our"},{"surface":"காமத்துப்","parts":[{"text":"காமத்துப்","lemma":"காமத்துப்","gloss":"of love"}],"gloss":"of love","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பகையே","parts":[{"text":"பகை","lemma":"pakai","gloss":"affliction"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"the affliction indeed"}]}],"literal":"And the root, and the trunk, and the branch, together / as if bound, hanging and linked continuously, / like hanging low down, of the jackfruit tree with fruit-bearing roots, / the lord of the mountain of roaring waterfalls, whenever he comes, [it] comes, / even if he departs, without leaving, / contends, O friend, our love's affliction.","translation":"O friend! Like the jackfruit tree whose heavy fruits hang in clusters, linked together from root to trunk to branch, hanging low to the ground, the pain of our love comes whenever the lord of the roaring mountain waterfalls arrives. And even when he departs, it does not leave us, but remains to torment us.","modern":"தோழியே! வேர், அடிமரம், கிளை ஆகிய அனைத்து இடங்களிலும் ஒன்றாகத் தொடுக்கப்பட்டது போல, ஒன்றோடொன்று தொடர்ந்து தொங்கி, தரையளவுக்குத் தாழ்ந்து கிடக்கும் பலாப்பழங்களைக் கொண்ட, ஆரவாரம் மிக்க அருவிகள் உடைய மலைநாட்டிற்குரிய தலைவன் வரும்போதெல்லாம் நம் காம நோய் நமக்கு வருகிறது. அவன் நம்மை விட்டுப் பிரிந்து சென்றாலும், அது நம்மை விட்டு நீங்காமல் நம்முடன் மாறுபட்டு நின்று வருத்துகிறது.","explanation":"The heroine speaks to her confidante about the overwhelming nature of her love-sickness. She compares her affliction to the heavy jackfruits that hang in continuous, dense clusters from the roots, trunk, and branches of the mountain trees. This vivid imagery belongs to the kuriñci landscape, representing the fertile, heavy, and inescapable nature of her passion. Just as the jackfruits are bound to every part of the tree, her pain is bound to her entire being. It intensifies whenever her lover arrives, and yet it refuses to leave her even when he departs.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}